{title: 444 - I'm a Pilgrim}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #444 • IM A PILGRIM • 9.11.9.10}
{lyricist: Mary S. B. Dana}
{composer: Arr. from an Italian air}
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 444}
{meta: tune IM A PILGRIM}
{meta: meter 9.11.9.10}
{meta: category Early Advent - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[F]I’m a pilgrim, and I’m a [C7]stranger;
[C7]I can [F]tarry, I can [C7/E]tarry but a [F]night;
[F]Do not [C]detain me, for [F]I am going
[F]To where the [C]fountains [Dm]are [Gm]ever [C]flowing.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[F]I'm a pilgrim, and I'm a [C7]stranger;
[C7]I can [F]tarry, I can [C7/E]tarry but a [F]night.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[F]There the glory is ever [C7]shining!
[C7]O, my [F]longing heart, my [C7/E]longing heart is [F]there;
[F]Here in [C]this country so dark [F]and dreary,
[F]I long have [C]wandered [Dm]forlorn [Gm]and [C]weary.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[F]There's the city to which I [C7]journey;
[C7]My Redeemer, [F]my Redeemer [C7]is its [F]light!
[F]There is [C]no sorrow, nor any [F]sighing,
[F]Nor any [C/E]tears [Dm]there, [Gm]or any [C]dying.
{end_of_verse}
